;
; AROS's Installer, started from an icon, looks for its script among the
; tooltypes of its OWN icon, not of the project double-clicked, so an
; Install icon cannot hand it the script. This file is what the AROS
; archives call Install: its icon runs it through IconX, in the drawer
; of the package, and the Installer gets the script on its command line.
;
; Before it, the processor: exec.library names it ("raspi-aarch64" on a
; Raspberry Pi), and the script finds ENV:EdgeSnapARM or ENV:EdgeSnapX86
; with nothing but (exists). After it, what that Installer's (run) cannot
; do, since it knows neither the command path nor a redirection: stop
; the copy running, let its library go and start the one just installed
; - only when the script got to its end and left T:EdgeSnapInstalled.
; IconX's Shell has only the basic command path, and the Installer is not
; in the same place everywhere: SYS:Utilities on AROS as built (the
; Raspberry Pi), C: on AROS One.
Version >ENV:EdgeSnapCPU exec.library FULL
Search >NIL: ENV:EdgeSnapCPU aarch64 QUIET
If WARN
  Echo >ENV:EdgeSnapX86 x86_64
Else
  Echo >ENV:EdgeSnapARM aarch64
EndIf
If EXISTS SYS:Utilities/Installer
  SYS:Utilities/Installer SCRIPT Install.script APPNAME EdgeSnap
Else
  If EXISTS C:Installer
    C:Installer SCRIPT Install.script APPNAME EdgeSnap
  Else
    Installer SCRIPT Install.script APPNAME EdgeSnap
  EndIf
EndIf
Delete >NIL: ENV:EdgeSnapCPU QUIET
If EXISTS T:EdgeSnapInstalled
  Delete >NIL: T:EdgeSnapInstalled QUIET
  SYS:WBStartup/EdgeSnap >NIL: QUIT
  Wait 2
  ; Avail FLUSH lets an older library go, but on AROS aarch64 Avail
  ; dies with an illegal instruction (nightly 20261005, QEMU raspi3b):
  ; there an update takes full effect at the next boot.
  If EXISTS ENV:EdgeSnapX86
    Avail >NIL: FLUSH
  EndIf
  If EXISTS C:WBRun
    C:WBRun SYS:WBStartup/EdgeSnap
  Else
    Run >NIL: <NIL: SYS:WBStartup/EdgeSnap
  EndIf
EndIf
Delete >NIL: ENV:EdgeSnapARM ENV:EdgeSnapX86 QUIET
